ologies into the building and fire  code is complex new york city loves  distributed generation but even though  we had a permit to install the micro  turbines no one told that to the fire  officer who showed up to permit our use  of the micro turbines to him it was a  hazard they wasn't familiar with and  would no way allow it to be turned on  calls replaced inquiries were made and  the fire department of New York pledged  to write rules and micro turbines this  took almost three years and so by the  time we did get it on it was already  broken a couple of years after finishing  the hellena we opened the epic at 125  West 31st Street also by FX foul a 400  unit rental building that shares space  with a friary for the Franciscan  brothers and an American Cancer Society  Hope Lodge the epic is LEED Gold and  while our other sustainable buildings  were filled with innovative technology  epic achieves lead quietly  cost-effectively by focusing on  materials and technologies that by the  top that by this time became easy to  source and use everyone asked about the  costs of building green which in my  opinion is a dumb question no one asks  how much more expensive it is to build a  building with elevators or air  conditioning the green features pay for  themselves  the real cost is the time it takes for  the planning effort and investigation  that must be done but in this effort  many of our building practices that were  considered green or a way to conserve  resources has become ingrained into the  work habits of our employees I'm  fortunate to work with great people who  truly care as much about the environment  as I do we now have a couple of very  exciting projects in the hopper next  year will break ground on our first  hotel project as you can see we don't  yet have a final design for the project  but we're working with cookplus Fox who  design one brian park and we expect it  to be an arresting design hopefully it  won't tip over to next door to the  hellena on W